  "narrative": "<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Short impact summary</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Images of Immigrants and Refugees (2019), published by Leuven University Press, has been cited 4 times. Beyond that, it has been downloaded 10,860 times.</p>\n<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Full narrative</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Images of Immigrants and Refugees by Leen d\u2019Haenens, Willem Joris and Fran\u00e7ois Heinderyckx was published by Leuven University Press in 2019. It is part of the Images of immigrants and refugees in Western Europe. Media representations, public opinion, and refugees\u2019 experiences, Chapt. 2, (21-36) series. Conceptually, the work connects to Geography, Political science, Regional science and Economic geography.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">OpenAlex records 4 citations. Citations peaked in 2019 with 1 citing works. Notable citing venues include Journal of Arab & Muslim Media Research, Journal of Ethnic and Migration Studies and Comparative Population Studies. They come from 5 countries, led by Belgium, Bulgaria and Germany.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">It has been downloaded 10,860 times via OAPEN. It is recorded in 1 library collection. Its subject matter aligns with Reduced inequalities among the Sustainable Development Goals. The work was funded by KU Leuven and Belgian Federal Science Policy Office.</p>",
